NNAAMMEE
     ggggaatteedd — GEOM Gate network daemon

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ggggaatteedd [--hh] [--nn] [--vv] [--aa _a_d_d_r_e_s_s] [--pp _p_o_r_t] [--FF _p_i_d_f_i_l_e] [--RR _r_c_v_b_u_f]
            [--SS _s_n_d_b_u_f] [_e_x_p_o_r_t_s _f_i_l_e]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The ggggaatteedd utility is a network server for the GEOM Gate class.  It runs
     on a server machine to service GEOM Gate requests from workers placed on
     a client machine.  Keep in mind, that connections between ggatec(8) and
     ggggaatteedd are not encrypted.

     Available options:

     --aa _a_d_d_r_e_s_s    Specifies an IP address to bind to.

     --hh            Print available options.

     --nn            Do not use TCP_NODELAY option on TCP sockets.

     --pp _p_o_r_t       Port on which ggggaatteedd listens for connections.  Default is
                   3080.

     --FF _p_i_d_f_i_l_e    PID file that ggggaatteedd uses.

     --RR _r_c_v_b_u_f     Size of receive buffer to use.  Default is 131072 (128kB).

     --SS _s_n_d_b_u_f     Size of send buffer to use.  Default is 131072 (128kB).

     --vv            Do not fork, run in foreground and print debug information
                   on standard output.

     _e_x_p_o_r_t_s _f_i_l_e  An alternate location for the exports file.

     The format of an exports file is as follows:

           1.2.3.4         RO      /dev/cd0
           1.2.3.0/24      RW      /tmp/test.img
           hostname        WO      /tmp/image

FFIILLEESS
     /var/run/ggated.pid  The default location of the ggggaatteedd PID file.

EEXXIITT SSTTAATTUUSS
     Exit status is 0 on success, or 1 if the command fails.  To get details
     about the failure, ggggaatteedd should be called with the --vv option.

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     Export CD-ROM device and a file:

           # echo "1.2.3.0/24 RO /dev/cd0" > /etc/gg.exports
           # echo "client RW /image" >> /etc/gg.exports
           # ggated

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     geom(4), ggatec(8), ggatel(8)

HHIISSTTOORRYY
     The ggggaatteedd utility appeared in FreeBSD 5.3.

